an't seem to see  eye-to-eye which is one of the many  reasons why hype house is splitting up  House members are forced to film a  minimum of three tic toc videos every  single day while juggling an education  and a social life nobody's got time for  that  things started to get ugly between Daisy  chase and Thomas when Daisy began  voicing her desire to be recognized as  the mansion's third co-founder she even  took to Instagram to give fans a  heads-up on what was really going on  according to Daisy when you start loving  yourself loudly and setting healthy  boundaries you're gonna piss off any  toxic people around you so clearly Daisy  is waving the red toxic flag in Thomas's  face and he's far from thrilled Daisy  ended her post by reminding fans to  never let them walk all over you but  what exactly went down between them and  why are legal actions being taken during  an interview with insider Daisy's lawyer  Chris Young revealed that Daisy is  officially leaving hypeeee house he also  stated that the tic-tock her plans to  create her own creator collective  however Chris explained that since  ongoing trademark disputes were afoot he  could not reveal whether or not Daisy  was allowed to use the heighth house  name but regardless not having a claim  to the hype house name won't stop her  from establishing a tick-tock collective  of her own but most surprising is the  revelation that Daisy is already in  talks with some of her fellow hype House  members and they're ready to jump ship  with her  turns out the hype house has little love  for Thomas Petro who had been pegged as  a tick-tock tyrant before we reveal  which tick stalkers have agreed to join  Daisy's cause let's talk about the root  of Daisy's legal battle and which  incident led her to confront Thomas  during a shoot Chris Young told insider  that Daisy is the reason tick stalkers  are allowed to rent the hype house in  the first place at the time the lease  was signed Daisy was the only one who  could qualify based on income so her  name is one of the few on the lease  Daisy revealed that she has received  zero recognition for her contributions  despite being a co-founder during the  same interview it was said that Daisy  and Thomas had been the ones who came up  with the concept for the tic-tock  mansion however dreams became a reality  when Thomas met chase but the pair never  praised Daisy for her contributions nor  did they include her in any of the  conversations back in January 2020 Daisy  filed three applications to trademark  the hype house and drama hit the fan in  February when Thomas used  trademark in an Instagram story  promoting hype House merchandise without  Daisy's consent  that's when Daisy's lawyers sent Thomas  a cease and desist letter  unfortunately Thomas chose to ignore  this letter and promoted hype House  merchandise anyway and well that's when  things got ugly between the tick talkers  in early March Daisy confronted Thomas  during a shoot leading to a verbal  altercation between the two  collaborators on top of using the high  post trademark Thomas gave contractors  the okay to make renovations without  consulting the landlord which puts  Daisy's deposit at risk and most  recently Daisy revealed that Thomas was  trying to rally other members of the  house against her to intimidate her from  coming into her own property well two  can play at that game we previously  mentioned that Daisy was recruiting hype  House members of her own many of the  House members have flocked to her side  however no concrete names have been  announced what we do know though is that  multiple tick tock errs have been  unfollowed by the group shared Instagram  account so far these members are Patrick  Houston Connor Yates Calvin Goldie and  Wyatt Xavier but what about group  members like the D'Amelio sisters  Addison Rey and a vani Greg for now none  of the young ladies have commented on  this split however secrets are bound to  be spilled sooner than later  it looks like older House members are  bumping heads with Thomas whereas  younger members are choosing to stay  away from the drama 20 year old Daisy  who is well known for having the first  certified real booty has added the label  of hype House co-founder to her  Instagram bio but while Daisy's claims  are justifiable internet trolls are  still bashing her for causing a rift in  the hype house type House isn't the  first creator collective to experience  legal trouble so early in the game  Jake Paul's team 10 and other social  media mansions have also encountered  bumps in the road when attempting  similar pursuits in the end having a  house full of teenagers can be quite the  uphill battle during an exclusive with  savanah sellers Alex Warren explained  that the house has a lot of group  meetings because teenagers have to  express their feelings so clearly the  House members are used to bumping heads  the seams you know we argue we fight we  have our differences but at the end of  the day we all go to bed we still love  each other  Alex also revealed that the group  doesn't have a lot of free time  he stated that they haven't used the  pool for fun since moving in in the end  everything is about making videos which  can take the fun out of tick-tock and  while it looks like the fame and drama  is getting out of hand and  unsurprisingly Thomas Petro is in over  his head  in early March Thomas shared a worrying  post on his Instagram story saying that  his anxiety was so bad he was going to  get sick this came right after Thomas  announced that his personal Instagram  page had been hacked fans were quick to  point a finger at Daisy Keach and so was  Thomas he blamed her for the hacking  without naming her telling his followers  that someone had paid to have him hacked  Daisy who has previously had access to  the hype house accounts password had  been locked out by Thomas and Lil hoodie  just a couple of days before the  incident took place on top of getting  hacked Thomas also revealed that the  hacker had tried to get into his PayPal  venmo cash app and bank account in an  attempt to steal all of his money Thomas  has since then stopped following Daisy  on his personal Instagram page amidst  all the drama  Charlie D'Amelio guest-starred on The  Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon where  she talked about what was really going  on in the hype house according to  Charlie the secret to her fame is being  authentic the tick-tock er told Jimmy  that she doesn't post videos when she's  not in the mood because she wants her  smiles to be as genuine as possible  however tick-tock errs have to upload up  to four videos a day to remain in good  standing with the hype house's strict  rule book for now Charlie has yet to  comment on the height house's legal  battles she's not choosing sides or  delving into the topic but she did  reveal that a lot is in the works for  her and her sister and she told her fans  to stay tuned for updates during an  interview with today sippy Anna sellers  asked the House members if they were  ever exhausted by the level of fame they  had attained and the crew quickly  revealed that they felt a little  overwhelmed  Avani Gregg told Savannah that they're  constantly attacked online for every  little mistake they make the members  looked exhausted and unhappy as they  talked about their daily filming  schedules Thomas chimed in saying that  living in hype house was like living on  a movie  said it never stopped said the founder  and well cover can attest to that  she told Savannah that she wakes up to  the people filming videos on her balcony  in the morning Thomas chimed in saying  that they have a house of 20 people  posting three to four times a day  trading a total of a hundred and fifty  videos on the daily yeah that map  doesn't quite add up but regardless it  just goes to show how exhausted everyone  is at the hype house Avani also revealed  that she doesn't live in the mansion  full-time because if she did she would  never get any of her homework done in  the end the hype house isn't a place for  a rest  it's a place where famous stick talkers  go to create new content for their fans  but while it's all smiles and games on  social media things are falling apart  behind the scenes  Daisy Keats refuses to stay silent any  longer and hype House members are  flocking to her side for now it looks  like Patrick Connor Calvin and Wyatt are  standing behind their girl Daisy however  most of the other hype House members  have refused to comment on the entire  situation despite all the legal battles  Daisy is hard at work trying to create a  hype house of her own however the name  of her mansion is subject to change  depending on how the legal battles turn  out do you think Daisy should start her  own creator collective or are these  stars taking the fun out of tick tock by  turning it into a business sound off in  the comments thanks for watching for  more fun videos be sure to subscribe to  the things and don't forget to give this  video a big thumbs up we'll see you next  time  you

